# Build context exclusions for the production images.
#
# Without this the context carries ~1.7GB of gitignored speech weights and every
# node_modules tree, which makes `docker build` look hung before it has read a
# single instruction.
#
# Note what is deliberately NOT excluded: apps/web/public. Its `worklets/`
# subdirectory is generated by web's `prebuild` step INSIDE the builder stage and
# is gitignored, so the runner stage copies public/ from the builder rather than
# from this context.

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Build output — every image builds its own inside the container.
**/dist
**/.next
**/.output
**/.turbo
.turbo
**/coverage
# Any name, not just tsconfig.tsbuildinfo: apps/api emits
# tsconfig.build.tsbuildinfo, and a host copy of it makes tsc believe the build
# is current, emit nothing, and leave the image with no dist at all.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# 1.7GB of gitignored model weights. Bind-mounted at run time, never baked in.
services/*/models
services/*/.venv

# Never let a real secret enter a build context.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
prod.env

# Agent tooling and working documents — no image needs them.
.claude
.agentkit
kits
plans
docs
benchmarks
.vscode

*.log
